WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.400
When a $9 million movie makes over&nbsp;
$150 million at the box office, you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.920
bet that movie's getting a sequel. Luckily, the&nbsp;
surprise 2019 hit "Escape Room" left things all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.400
set up for a follow-up, coming this summer&nbsp;
in "Escape Room: Tournament of Champions."

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.120
The first "Escape Room" hit theaters in&nbsp;
January 2019, where it turned a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.160
profit in the face of little opposition. With&nbsp;
that kind of success, few were surprised when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.640
it was announced the next month that work had&nbsp;
already begun on a sequel to "Escape Room."

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:35.520
Deadline reported that studio Sony Pictures&nbsp;
Releasing had tapped director Adam Robitel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.240
two of his creative colleagues on the movie,&nbsp;
screenwriter Bragi F. Schut and producer Neal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:46.320
H. Moritz, to get to work on "Escape Room 2,"&nbsp;
tentatively set for release on April 17, 2020.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.280
Sony executives were evidently blown away by&nbsp;
the film's success. The first "Escape Room"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:57.360
received only modest compliments from viewers&nbsp;
-- as of June 2021, the first movie has a 51%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:02.640
ranking from critics and audiences both. But&nbsp;
the fact that the movie made so much money in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.320
spite of those middling reviews made it an easy&nbsp;
decision to greenlight and fast-track a sequel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.240
After all, it's not every day that a&nbsp;
movie made for less than $10 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.600
makes more than 15 times that&nbsp;
amount at the box office.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.320
Two months went by before anyone heard much&nbsp;
else about the impending "Escape Room" movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:25.440
Then, in April 2019, Robitel sat down for an&nbsp;
exclusive interview with Bloody Disgusting and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.560
gave audiences their first hint of where the&nbsp;
sequel might be going. That includes expanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:35.360
the mythology behind the evil Minos organization&nbsp;
behind the original movie's escape room, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.680
he referred to as a Machiavellian company that&nbsp;
knows everything about you. The filmmaker said,

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.080
"It was tough admittedly to pull back the&nbsp;
veil and I know some people are like oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.800
this is about rich people watching people get&nbsp;
killed, but there’s some cool mythology that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.120
we’re trying to bring in the second movie. I&nbsp;
think the fact that they could hijack a plane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.600
whether it’s literal or figurative, there’s&nbsp;
something cool about that. It’s pushed for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.960
sure but we think hopefully the&nbsp;
audience is going for the ride."

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.080
"This is way bigger than last time."

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.840
"We've gotta try something, right?"

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.240
"N-no, no, no!"

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:14.480
The Hollywood landscape may be littered&nbsp;
with sequels, remakes, spinoffs, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.120
cinematic universes, but the fact remains that&nbsp;
it's actually pretty hard to make that first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.000
sequel to a movie. You're essentially trying to&nbsp;
simultaneously recapture lightning in a bottle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.840
and expand on an existing story in a way that&nbsp;
not only makes sense but is also entertaining.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:35.280
One wrong move can spell the difference between&nbsp;
a one-off sequel and a full-blown franchise.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.800
All that considered, it's not too&nbsp;
surprising to hear director Adam Robitel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.160
confess that the "Tournament of&nbsp;
Champions" filmmakers faced some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.320
creative challenges in the early days of&nbsp;
development on their "Escape Room" sequel.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.560
Robitel explained to Bloody Disgusting&nbsp;
that the biggest obstacle to overcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.560
was deciding what type of escape rooms&nbsp;
to include in the sequel since the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.080
movie already utilized a lot&nbsp;
of different themes. He said,

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.680
"We did fire, gravity, ice, cold, gas so we&nbsp;
need to outdo ourselves now. [...] We have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.080
some really cool stuff we're developing, and&nbsp;
hopefully the audience will think that way too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.520
but it's tougher. We did do the&nbsp;
greatest hits in the first movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.120
so the road gets narrower as it goes&nbsp;
on. How do you give the audience what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.600
they're expecting from an 'Escape Room'&nbsp;
movie but also not the exact same thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.920
that the first movie did? So we're really&nbsp;
trying to iron all that out right now."

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.920
Thankfully, it took only a few months&nbsp;
for the minds behind "Escape Room:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.960
Tournament of Champions" to sort&nbsp;
everything out and settle on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.320
script that they were pleased with.&nbsp;
Once they reached that milestone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:38.720
the next order of business was auditioning and&nbsp;
selecting actors to be in the sequel's cast.

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:43.680
There were six players in the original "Escape&nbsp;
Room" film. However, as is normal for a movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:47.760
like this, all six players don't manage to&nbsp;
survive the game. In fact, only two of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.960
six members of the group manage to escape: Taylor&nbsp;
Russell as Zoey, and Logan Miller as Ben. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:58.240
process of surviving the game, the unlikely&nbsp;
duo uncovers a vast corporate conspiracy that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:03.680
involves high-stakes betting on who, if any, of&nbsp;
the players might make it out of the game alive.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.360
Both of those characters will be back for&nbsp;
the "Escape Room" sequel with Russell and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.920
Miller reprising their respective roles.&nbsp;
That's not really a shock seeing as though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.760
their return is essentially set up in&nbsp;
the final moments of "Escape Room."

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.120
Since a new game is officially&nbsp;
afoot for "Tournament of Champions,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.600
new faces will be joining Zoey and&nbsp;
Ben. Thomas Cocquerel will play Nathan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:29.280
"Teen Wolf" alum Holland Roden will portray&nbsp;
Rachel, and Indya Moore of "Pose" fame is set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.600
for the role of Brianna, while "Orphan"&nbsp;
breakout Isabelle Fuhrman and "Step Up:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.920
High Water's" Carlito Olivero round&nbsp;
out the game's roster of six players.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.000
As for who these characters are,&nbsp;
well, the title of the sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.680
sort of spills the beans there:&nbsp;
They're all winners of past games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.760
brought back for a championship tournament&nbsp;
to determine who's the best of the bunch.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.080
"No, no, no."

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.360
"It's happening again?"

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.040
"You guys have played the game before?"

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.760
"So what is this? Like a tournament of champions?"

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:03.600
Details on each character beyond Zoey and Ben are&nbsp;
scarce for right now, though director Adam Robitel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.480
did tell CinemaBlend that each champion will have&nbsp;
a mysterious backstory pertaining to the struggles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.720
they went through prior to their involvement&nbsp;
in the Tournament of Champions. He said,

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.640
"What I try to do is set up questions for&nbsp;
each of them, like I did in the first movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:22.080
We're leaning into, 'Why does this person&nbsp;
have a scar?' and 'Why is this guy seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.120
reading the last rites to somebody?' There's one&nbsp;
character who has […] an anomalous immune system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.920
and so there's weird things that happen with&nbsp;
pain. And so we're setting up all these questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.720
[proving] that they're not&nbsp;
your average characters."

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.520
"I can't feel physical pain. Just imagine the&nbsp;
kinds of puzzles they came up with for me."

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.960
Way back when "Escape Room 2" was first&nbsp;
announced, Sony Pictures Releasing stamped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:50.320
it with an April 17, 2020 release date. At&nbsp;
the time, it seemed like a perfect debut date:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.400
v time between the first and second&nbsp;
movies to allow hype to build, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:58.000
launching it in the spring rather than the&nbsp;
summer meant there wouldn't be the risk of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.200
massive tentpole productions&nbsp;
crushing it at the box office.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.560
But, of course, "Escape Room:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.680
Tournament of Champions" never did&nbsp;
arrive in theaters on that day.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.000
After multiple delays, "Escape Room: Tournament&nbsp;
of Champions" was shuffled around multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:15.840
release dates in 2020, then 2021, before&nbsp;
finally landing all the way in January 7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.560
2022. But then, In April 2021,&nbsp;
Deadline reported that the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:25.040
was moving back through time to land&nbsp;
in theaters later that year on July 16.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:29.840
Viewers in Australia can see the film even&nbsp;
earlier, as it opens down under on July 1.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.600
When we last saw Zoey and Ben,&nbsp;
they made a pact to confront&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:37.760
the masterminds of the first movie's&nbsp;
deadly game. But as the audience saw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.840
those mysterious master game makers&nbsp;
were already a few steps ahead of them.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:46.160
The final moments of "Escape Room" teased&nbsp;
that the organization's shadowy mastermind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.560
was already plotting a new, near-impossible&nbsp;
to survive game to be played on the duo's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:54.720
flight to New York. From the "Tournament of&nbsp;
Champions" trailer, it seems Zoey and Ben&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.240
either survived or dodged that game en route to&nbsp;
New York. They still get ensnared in a new game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:04.000
though, and this one opens on a subway&nbsp;
car with a handful of strangers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.480
As alluded to in the film's title, those&nbsp;
strangers are all survivors of past games.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:15.840
"It's the finals of the Jeopardy!&nbsp;
Tournament of Champions."

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:17.680
"It's mine!"

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:21.680
According to returning director&nbsp;
Adam Robitel, "Escape Room:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:25.920
Tournament of Champions" will reveal that&nbsp;
the scale of Minos' organization is far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.920
larger than even the first movie&nbsp;
hinted at. He told CinemaBlend,

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.560
"What we're going to realize&nbsp;
is that on any given day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.680
there are multiple games&nbsp;
happening all around the world."

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:39.280
By bringing back Zoey, Ben, and a&nbsp;
group of other champions to face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:43.120
the dangers of an escape room again,&nbsp;
Robitel also noted of the sequel,

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.160
"It's sort of a meditation on trauma, and&nbsp;
how people deal with trauma. But also,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.960
what they've learned through&nbsp;
their first trial by fire."

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:53.840
While "Escape Room: Tournament&nbsp;
of Champions" doesn't appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:57.680
to be venturing too far from the first&nbsp;
film's formula, from the look of things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.640
the filmmakers have really outdone themselves&nbsp;
in terms of both game and production design.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:07.280
The sequel will presumably have its fair&nbsp;
share of shocking twists and reveals too.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:11.040
As for who's going to make it&nbsp;
out of the new game unscathed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.520
your guess is as good as ours. With "Escape Room:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.920
Tournament of Champions" hitting theaters in&nbsp;
mere weeks, we'll all find out soon enough.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.600
If you can't make it to the theater when "Escape&nbsp;
Room: Tournament of Champions" debuts on July 16,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.360
you may be wondering whether the film will&nbsp;
have a simultaneous streaming release like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:32.080
many other movies have this year. The&nbsp;
answer is, sadly, pretty disappointing:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:36.400
"Escape Room" Tournament of Champions" isn't&nbsp;
going to be streaming anywhere any time soon.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:41.040
Adam Robitel explained the decision when&nbsp;
speaking with CinemaBlend in May 2021.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:45.360
In the director's opinion, horror movies&nbsp;
should be seen in theaters, where it's dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:50.320
quiet, and free from outside distractions&nbsp;
- the perfect environment to be scared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.920
out of your mind. He put an artful&nbsp;
spin on the subject, sharing,

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.480
"The Latin root of the word horror means&nbsp;
'to bristle on the back of the neck.'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.440
It's the one genre that has a physical and&nbsp;
physiological influence over the audience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:08.080
It's manipulating them. People love to be&nbsp;
afraid in groups. They love to go on dates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.400
to scream and grab their popcorn."

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.560
"Escape Room: Tournament of Champions" will likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:16.320
be available to watch from the comfort&nbsp;
of your own home sometime in the future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:21.280
but for now, you'll just have to head to&nbsp;
the cinema to see it, starting on July 16.

